WEBVTT

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:05.716
[Stoick] No dragon or Viking sets foot off
this island until I give the word!

00:00:05.883 --> 00:00:08.052
Wait, because some guy you
knew is stirring up trouble

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:09.720
in some faraway land?

00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:12.056
Because Drago Bludvist is a madman

00:00:12.181 --> 00:00:14.391
without conscience or mercy.

00:00:14.558 --> 00:00:18.854
And if he's built a dragon army,
gods help us all.

00:00:18.979 --> 00:00:20.940
Get them into their pens! Quickly!

00:00:21.106 --> 00:00:22.942
Then, let's ride back out there.

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:25.194
We'll follow those trappers to Drago

00:00:25.277 --> 00:00:26.528
and talk some sense into him.

00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:28.405
No. We fortify the island.

00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:30.115
It's our duty to keep the peace!

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:33.661
Peace is over, Hiccup.
I must prepare you for war.

00:00:33.827 --> 00:00:34.870
War?

00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:37.539
Dad, if Drago is coming for our dragons,

00:00:37.665 --> 00:00:40.084
we can't wait around for him to get here.

00:00:40.251 --> 00:00:43.295
Let's go find him and change his mind.

00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:45.506
No, some minds won't be changed, Hiccup.

00:00:45.673 --> 00:00:47.925
Berk is what you need to worry about.

00:00:48.092 --> 00:00:50.469
A chief protects his own.

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:54.431
[Stoick] Secure the stables!
Latch every stall!

00:00:54.598 --> 00:00:56.517
-Hiccup, don't!
-I have to.

00:00:56.684 --> 00:00:57.726
[Stoick] This way!

00:00:57.893 --> 00:00:59.478
-Quickly!
-[Toothless screeches]

00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:02.356
[Stoick] Hiccup!

00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:03.983
[people shouting indistinctly]

00:01:04.066 --> 00:01:05.109
Come on!

00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:08.487
Hiccup!

00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:14.535
[sighs]

00:01:18.872 --> 00:01:21.000
Keep your eyes peeled, lads!

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:23.877
With this wind,
we'll reach Drago by daybreak,

00:01:24.044 --> 00:01:27.548
so best we fill this ship up
with dragons, and quick!

00:01:27.756 --> 00:01:29.300
It's no time to be picky.

00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:30.509
Uh… Eret?

00:01:30.592 --> 00:01:32.261
Not if we want to keep our…

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.515
Heads! Off the port quarter!

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.892
Net them, lads! Take them down!

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.481
You're not getting away this time.

00:01:45.024 --> 00:01:46.025
Fire!

00:01:47.276 --> 00:01:48.694
Reload!

00:01:48.861 --> 00:01:50.529
[trapper] Reload! Incoming!

00:01:53.282 --> 00:01:54.283
[Eret] And here I was,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.618
worried we might turn up empty-handed.

00:01:56.785 --> 00:01:58.579
Nope. It's your lucky day.

00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:00.331
-[gasps]
-We give up.

00:02:01.957 --> 00:02:05.836
That's one Night Fury, one Deadly Nadder,

00:02:06.003 --> 00:02:09.006
and two of the finest
dragon riders west of Luk Tuk.

00:02:09.256 --> 00:02:11.467
That ought to make the boss happy, right?

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.302
-[growls]
-Excuse us.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.513
-[Astrid whispers] What are you doing?
-Toothless, stay.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.601
Uh, the dragons don't
care for cramped spaces,

00:02:20.684 --> 00:02:22.186
so they'll just hang out with you.

00:02:22.352 --> 00:02:23.896
They won't be any trouble.

00:02:23.979 --> 00:02:25.314
[trappers snarl]

00:02:25.397 --> 00:02:27.107
Unless you do that.

00:02:27.274 --> 00:02:31.236
You know, wooden boat, big
ocean. How is your swimming?

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.321
Not good.

00:02:32.404 --> 00:02:33.405
[sighs]

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:34.573
[all gasp]

00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:38.202
Oops! Almost forgot.
You can't have armed prisoners.

00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:39.953
How is this a plan?

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.790
Just what every dragon trapper needs.

00:02:42.915 --> 00:02:46.168
One end coats the blade
in Monstrous Nightmare saliva.

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:49.004
The other sprays Hideous Zippleback gas.

00:02:49.213 --> 00:02:51.882
All it takes is a spark, and…

00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:53.008
[explosion]

00:02:53.092 --> 00:02:54.134
[trappers yell]

00:02:54.218 --> 00:02:56.386
-[Hiccup] Yeah, there you go.
-[trappers coughing]

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.514
[Hiccup] Once they see you
as one of their own,

00:02:58.597 --> 00:03:01.183
even the testiest dragons
can be trained. Right, bud?

00:03:01.266 --> 00:03:03.268
Give me that! [grunts]

00:03:04.144 --> 00:03:06.105
What game are you playing?

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.273
[Hiccup] No game.
We just wanna meet Drago.

00:03:08.357 --> 00:03:09.399
[grunts] Why?

00:03:09.566 --> 00:03:12.402
Because I'm going
to change his mind about dragons.

00:03:12.528 --> 00:03:13.946
[trappers laughing]

00:03:16.073 --> 00:03:18.033
He can be really persuasive.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.493
Once you've earned his loyalty,

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:22.162
there is nothing
a dragon won't do for you.

00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:25.374
[blows raspberry] You won't be
changing any minds around here.

00:03:25.541 --> 00:03:26.917
I can change yours.

00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:29.002
Right here. Right now.

00:03:31.588 --> 00:03:33.132
Uh… May I?

00:03:37.803 --> 00:03:39.429
Dragon riders!

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:45.144
[snarls]

00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:46.270
Huh?

00:03:46.353 --> 00:03:47.437
[Hiccup] Put me down!

00:03:47.604 --> 00:03:49.815
Snotlout, what are you doing?

00:03:49.898 --> 00:03:51.567
See how well I protect and provide?

00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:52.609
[groans]

00:03:52.693 --> 00:03:54.194
-[gasps]
-What is with all the nets?

00:03:54.278 --> 00:03:55.696
[Ruffnut] Hey, watch it! That was…

00:03:55.863 --> 00:03:58.240
Close.

00:04:00.951 --> 00:04:03.245
Oh, my.

00:04:05.956 --> 00:04:08.250
Me likey.

00:04:11.795 --> 00:04:13.297
Take me.

00:04:14.756 --> 00:04:15.924
[grunts]

00:04:17.176 --> 00:04:18.468
Hold your fire! [grunts]

00:04:22.055 --> 00:04:25.017
[grunts] What are you guys doing here?

00:04:25.184 --> 00:04:27.227
We're here to rescue you!

00:04:27.394 --> 00:04:28.937
I don't need to be rescued!

00:04:29.104 --> 00:04:30.397
[Stoick] Enough!

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.278
Well, didn't you just pick the wrong ship?

00:04:36.486 --> 00:04:39.031
I am Eret, son of [muffled] Eret.

00:04:39.698 --> 00:04:41.658
[grunts] I'm…

00:04:42.993 --> 00:04:45.245
[straining] Get this thing off me.

00:04:45.412 --> 00:04:46.830
-Anyone else?
-[Eret grunting]

00:04:47.873 --> 00:04:48.874
That's what I figured.

00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:52.002
You, saddle up. We're going home.

00:04:52.169 --> 00:04:53.170
No.

00:04:54.171 --> 00:04:55.923
Of all the irresponsible--

00:04:56.089 --> 00:04:58.884
I'm trying to protect our dragons
and stop a war!

00:04:59.051 --> 00:05:00.302
How is that irresponsible?

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.888
Because war is what he wants, son!

00:05:03.388 --> 00:05:04.848
[sighs]

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.268
[sighs]

00:05:08.936 --> 00:05:11.480
Years ago, there was
a great gathering of chieftains

00:05:11.688 --> 00:05:14.441
to discuss the dragon
scourge we all faced.

00:05:14.608 --> 00:05:18.904
Into our midst
came a stranger from a strange land,

00:05:19.071 --> 00:05:22.950
covered in scars
and draped in a cloak of dragon skin.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.911
He carried no weapon,

00:05:26.078 --> 00:05:28.830
and spoke softly, saying that he,

00:05:29.206 --> 00:05:32.709
Drago Bludvist, was a man of the people,

00:05:32.876 --> 00:05:37.214
devoted to freeing mankind
from the tyranny of dragons.

00:05:37.547 --> 00:05:39.675
He claimed that he alone
could control the dragons

00:05:39.841 --> 00:05:43.136
and that he alone could keep us safe,

00:05:43.303 --> 00:05:45.639
if we chose to bow down

00:05:45.722 --> 00:05:46.890
and follow him.

00:05:46.974 --> 00:05:47.975
[all laughing]

00:05:50.519 --> 00:05:52.521
-Stupid.
-Good one.

00:05:52.688 --> 00:05:54.773
Aye, we laughed, too.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.693
Until he wrapped
himself in his cloak and cried out,

00:05:57.859 --> 00:06:00.570
"Then see how well you do without me!"

00:06:01.613 --> 00:06:04.283
The rooftop suddenly burst into flames,

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:07.869
and from it, armored dragons descended,

00:06:08.328 --> 00:06:10.330
burning the hall to the ground.

00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:13.000
I…

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:16.712
was the only one to escape.

00:06:21.466 --> 00:06:25.262
Men who kill without reason
cannot be reasoned with.

00:06:25.429 --> 00:06:27.097
-Maybe.
-Hiccup!

00:06:27.264 --> 00:06:28.765
[Hiccup] I'm still going to try.

00:06:31.351 --> 00:06:32.853
This is what I'm good at.

00:06:32.978 --> 00:06:35.689
And if I could change your mind,

00:06:35.856 --> 00:06:37.566
I can change his, too.

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:40.277
Come on.

00:06:41.653 --> 00:06:42.779
-Let's go.
-[Stoick] No!

00:06:42.946 --> 00:06:44.948
Lead the others back to Berk.

00:06:45.115 --> 00:06:47.200
I've had enough mutiny for one day.

00:06:49.911 --> 00:06:52.289
Ooh, I like that.

00:06:52.372 --> 00:06:53.373
[Stoick] Ruffnut!

00:06:53.498 --> 00:06:55.167
[groans] Okay!

00:06:56.209 --> 00:06:57.794
-Ah!
-[grunting]

00:07:01.256 --> 00:07:02.257
Ugh!

00:07:10.182 --> 00:07:12.267
[screams in frustration]

00:07:14.728 --> 00:07:17.439
[sighs] Don't worry, bud.

00:07:17.773 --> 00:07:20.275
I'm not gonna let anything happen to you.

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:22.694
I promise.

00:07:22.778 --> 00:07:24.529
[Toothless grumbles]

00:07:30.369 --> 00:07:31.912
Oh, come on, Dad!

00:07:32.037 --> 00:07:33.372
Really?

00:07:41.755 --> 00:07:43.215
Okay.

00:07:43.924 --> 00:07:45.717
No sudden moves.

00:07:47.094 --> 00:07:48.762
[dragon screeching]

